From 9d1cdb99dfdbf1240cacecac29744449ba7305c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soaresden <soaresden@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:24:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fbs: let a user font stand in for the device system font

Adds system-font and system-font-scale options, exposed in the System
settings tab (font picker plus an Add button copying fonts into the
fonts folder, and a size percentage).

When set, the chosen user font is linked in front of every text face of
the ROM, sized so its capitals match the original face (scaled by the
percentage). This covers both the TrueType faces of S60 devices and the
bitmap .gdr faces of EKA1 devices such as the N-Gage.

- linked font adapter: per-component metric identifiers sized by
  capital height; sizes the text atlas asks for without going through
  get_nearest_supported_metric are scaled from a known one.
- antialiased component glyphs can be copied into an 8bpp (gdr) atlas.
